WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
  proof/mutation_matrix.out records 7 planted mutations, 7 caught RED, and it
  is a true record of those seven runs. It is not a complete one. Two of the
  fix's guarantees had NO test that could fail:

  GAP 1  the central behaviour. `return None` as the first statement of
         preparation._load_operator_config reinstates P14 exactly --
         prepare() stores config_path on the request and then ignores it.
  GAP 2  change site 7, the `config=load_config(...)` line in
         cli.main._qualify_one_profile -- the operations-parity limb the fix
         commit itself calls load-bearing ("carriage alone would have left all
         8 committed run-config.yaml files permanently unrunnable").

REPRODUCTION OF BOTH GAPS, BEFORE ANY TEST WAS WRITTEN
  (commands run in this worktree at a4f0d3ce2, tests/ unmodified)

  GAP 1, the two files the fix's own criterion names:
    $ python -m pytest tests/test_managed_path_config_read.py \
                       tests/test_run_preparation_service.py -q
      with `return None` planted : 23 passed in 93.05s

  GAP 1, the whole blast-radius ring (run_preparation_service,
  manifest_config_disclosure, reusable_qualification, single_run_path,
  v6_only_cli_admission, admission, v6_only_application_admission,
  managed_path_config_read):
      with `return None` planted : 217 passed, 1 skipped in 56.53s
      clean tree                 : 217 passed, 1 skipped in 58.11s
    -> byte-identical. Nothing anywhere goes red.

  GAP 2, change site 7 deleted (git diff --stat: 1 file changed, 1 deletion):
    $ python -m pytest tests/test_managed_path_config_read.py -q
                                 : 8 passed in 32.69s
    $ grep -rln "_qualify_one_profile" tests/
                                 : (no output; exit 1)
    -> the function had no test of any kind.

  Verifier's diagnosis confirmed: R1 monkeypatches RunPreparationService
  wholesale, so it can only prove the path reaches the request object and can
  never observe what prepare() does with it; R2-R8 call
  build_preparation_manifest / qualification_subject_manifest directly and
  never enter prepare() or either CLI verb. No test joined the two halves.

TESTS ADDED (tests/test_managed_path_config_read.py, alongside the eight)
  R9  test_prepare_compiles_the_run_from_the_operator_config_file
      Drives the REAL RunPreparationService.prepare() -- not monkeypatched --
      with a real run-config.yaml on disk, and asserts on the manifest AS
      WRITTEN to the run root: RESEARCH_BACKEND is CARRIED into the Config the
      run executes, JUDGE_SEATS_ENABLED is DISCLOSED by typed notice, and an
      unconfigured run of the same question through the same service shows
      neither limb and lands on a different root.
  R10 test_qualify_addresses_the_subject_the_configured_run_needs
      Calls cli.main._qualify_one_profile through a real parsed
      `--config F --provider-profile P qualify` argument namespace, on a home
      whose cache holds ONLY the configured subject, and asserts the verb
      addressed the subject a `reason --config F` run needs, reused it, and
      proposed zero provider calls.

